        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T16:27:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need this as a config setting? This sounds like a bug.",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d24c9d04_a2a2ce99",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054778
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T17:03:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Change Ib522a86 introduced an explicit test to ensure wrong case doesn\u0027t match.\nI guess it might be a legacy use case, however I am wanted to make sure to be back compatible.\n\n@ekempin@google.com do you recall what was the use case for that test?",
      "parentUuid": "ae4a0f6e_d08c7480",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44563834_917ac07b",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T22:13:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@nasser.grainawi@oss.qualcomm.com I believe this behaviour came from the transition of the accounts table into the `All-Users.git` repository, with the concept of having the e-mail as secondary id.\n\nIf you have User@Company.com and user@company.com in the external-ids, they will result in different notedb ids.\n\nHowever, Lucene returns case-insensitive matching, therefore @ekempin@google.com introduced a further check for exact matching as post-processing from Lucene.\n\nBottom line: we can\u0027t just _fix the bug_ as-is IMHO, as we\u0027ve been relying on this bug since Gerrit v2.14 (over 12 releases ago).",
      "parentUuid": "d24c9d04_a2a2ce99",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72049417_219b5fd9",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T09:40:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems the bug you are fixing here may break Gerrit\u0027s assumption that any given mailbox can be associated to at most one Gerrit account if there are multiple accounts using the same email address with different case.",
      "parentUuid": "44563834_917ac07b",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6ed2e18_9847023c",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T10:09:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, an email should never be owned by multiple accounts at the same time.",
      "parentUuid": "72049417_219b5fd9",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1debc29e_89e30e43",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T14:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but if e-mails with different case must be considered as different, Gerrit should allow two accounts (account1 and account2) having two e-mails that differ only in their case (account1 \u003d user@company.com; account2 \u003d User@company.com).\n\nThe above isn\u0027t allowed by Gerrit: two accounts cannot share the same e-mail even if they differ in their case.\n\nHere is the inconsistency:\na) Associating e-mails to accounts is done *case insensitive*\nb) Searching for accounts by e-mail is done *case sensitive*",
      "parentUuid": "e6ed2e18_9847023c",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2fd42f3_965383ba",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T07:45:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e a) Associating e-mails to accounts is done case insensitive\n\nI don\u0027t understand this. Aren\u0027t we just using the case that is provided to store the email?",
      "parentUuid": "1debc29e_89e30e43",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a7d0b55_7c2efcc5",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-11T08:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e a) Associating e-mails to accounts is done case insensitive\n\u003e \n\u003e I don\u0027t understand this. Aren\u0027t we just using the case that is provided to store the email?\n\nBefore the association, we look for duplicates with a case insensitive search.",
      "parentUuid": "b2fd42f3_965383ba",
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84ba64d1_30942f94",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T22:13:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is counter-intuitive: I would expect a feature to be enabled when you set a flag to true, but here we enable the case-insensitive matching when the flag is set to false.\n\nWe should be consistent with the approach we took for the case-insensitive username matching, see https://gerrit-documentation.storage.googleapis.com/Documentation/3.10.2/config-gerrit.html#auth.userNameCaseInsensitive",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "540594b3a695a0b74a6bbe7d13165df2c05e5bae",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9d3f65f6_52c30f4e",
        "filename": "Documentation/config-gerrit.txt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1054778
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-08T08:03:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Amended for consistency with other \"casing\" features.\n\n\u003e I would expect a feature to be enabled when you set a flag to true, but here we enable the case-insensitive matching when the flag is set to false.\n\nI think it depends on what you expect the feature to be. In this PS the feature was matching email in a case sensitive way. So it was correct enableing it by default.\n\n\u003e We should be consistent with the approach we took for the case-insensitive username matching, see https://gerrit-documentation.storage.googleapis.com/Documentation/3.10.2/config-gerrit.html#auth.userNameCaseInsensitive\n\nGood point.",
      "parentUuid": "84ba64d1_30942f94",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 18
      },
